timestamp=2026-11-04T20:36:56.709Z level=INFO run=73bb6740 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport csv\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/hospital_compensation_registry.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    rows = list(reader)\n\n# Also look for patients who might be deceased but don't have claims themselves\n# Common pattern: people who are emergency contacts of others but have no claims, or coverage status weird, etc.\n# Also those who show up as EC for someone else but their own row has no claim?\n\n# Build sets\nhas_claim = set()\nfor r in rows:\n    if r['record_date'] and r['record_date'].strip():\n        has_claim.add(r['patient_id'])\n\n# Who is listed as EC but has no claims?\nec_listed_no_claims = []\nfor r in rows:\n    ec = r['emergency_contact_patient_id']\n    if ec:\n        if ec not in has_claim:\n            ec_listed_no_claims.append(ec)\n\nfrom collections import Counter\nprint(Counter(ec_listed_no_claims).most_common(10))\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
